# sm115, the thrice-told farmhand (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 2: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle sm115
revision 2
state ready
dialect southmeadow
accent broad light
tier standard
written_for cty_alder_blossomcroft
written_by claude
title the thrice-told farmhand
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=farmer talk=chatty
traits temper=calm talk=chatty warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=content
quirk tells_the_same_three_stories
likes plum_tart long_walks market_bustle first_warm_day
dislikes bad_manners deep_mud
fears a_hard_winter_on_the_road
hopes to_finish_learning_the_scythe a_warm_spring_every_year
topics memories +0.5 pastimes +0.4 work +0.3 food +0.2 weather +0.2 gossip +0.1
styles comfort=talkative gossip=open refuse=plain tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# works the fields out of the granary, loud and in no hurry, with three good tales told so often the whole lane could finish every one, and an eye that drifts up the north road whenever winter comes.

words
oath! = Furrow and fair | By the long field
saying! = A good tale wants telling twice | The road comes round again
tart = plum tart | a slab of plum tart, still warm
walk = a long walk | a walk to nowhere much
market = the market | market day at its loudest
warmday = the first warm day | the first day you can leave your coat off
mud = deep mud | mud up to the hocks
manners = no manners | manners like a pig at a trough
uproad = the road north | the long road up past the barn
loft = the big barn | the granary loft
scythe = the scythe | the long scythe
tales = my three tales | the same three stories
ewe = the ewe | that daft ewe
pig = the prize pig | that great fat pig
farfield = the far field | the barley past the mill
fair = the summer fair | the fair

any
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : My week's #wages# won't fill a basket at the shop, and I've never once seen a shopkeeper go thin. #annoyed#.
opinion @1 houses against 1 : I've cut their fields year on year, and couldn't tell you what a single one of them looks like. Not once, #address#.
opinion @1 times against 1 : Every week's a notch harder, and nobody up at the big houses has noticed. #grumble#.
opinion @1 newcomers against 1 : #loft.capitalize# has work for so many and no more. Each newcomer's a share gone.
opinion @1 festivals for 1 : #fair.capitalize# brings every wolf in town out at once. I could talk all day. I do.
opinion @1 city against 1 : Ridgemere? I'd lose my way and my voice in a week. I'll keep to #uproad#'s near end.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#! You're new to me. Stop and talk, I've time. | #greet#, #address#! I don't know your face, but I'll know it now.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes self.job=farmer] : #greet#! Mind #scythe#, I swing wide. | #greet#! Grab a sheaf if you're stopping; I'll talk while we work.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : #greet#! You're up early too. So am I. | #greet#! Grey and cool. Best hour for #walk#.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#! Evening, and my legs know it. | #greet#. Late, but I'll still talk, #address#.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : There you are! I was just telling somebody about you. | Oh, it's you! Sit, sit. I've one of #tales# for you.
line @1 again.open : Twice today! #welcome_back#. | You again! Good. I'd more to say anyway.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#! | #greet#! Loud as ever, me.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : #greet#! Just the one I wanted. | #greet#! Sit down; I've news, or a story, or both.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : #greet#! Don't mind me, I talk with my paws busy. | #greet#! Keep up while I walk the row.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#! | #farewell#! I'll tell you the rest next time.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#! | #farewell#! Mind the ruts, #address#.
line @1 react.news : #oath#! That's one for the telling. | Well! I'll be telling that at #supper#, see if I don't.
line @1 react.news.new : #surprise#! I never heard that. | #marvel#! News to me, and I hear plenty.
line @1 react.news.known : #knew#. Had it at the granary this morning. | Heard it already! It came down the rows faster than the wind.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #doubt#. That sounds like one of my stories, and those grow. | Hm. I'll wait for an eye that saw it, #address#.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Oh, that's #bad#. #pity#. | That's a hard thing. I'm sorry for it, I am.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : #gladnews#! That wants telling round. | Oh, #good#! I'll be glad of that all day.
line @1 answer.how : Well! Loud and well, same as ever. #fine#. | #fine#. Legs tired, mouth not.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : #busy.capitalize#, but I can talk and work both. | Flat out, and still chattering, #address#.
line @1 ask.how : And you? Tell me everything. | How are you keeping, #address#? Go on, I'll listen for once.
line @1 sympathise : #sympathy#. Sit down by me a while. | Oh, that's #bad#. I'll be quiet, if you want quiet.
line @1 decline : #hedge#, I can't. #loft.capitalize# wants me till dark, and the farmer counts. | I'd love to. I can't. #account#, and it's a long row.
line @1 accept_decline : #no_matter#! Another day, then. | All right. It'll wait, same as my stories.
line @1 thank : #thanks#! | Thank you! I'll tell everybody you did that.
line @1 deflect_thanks : #deflect#! | It was nothing. I'd only have been telling #tales# otherwise.
line @1 preclose : #preclose#. | Well, I've talked your ear off. #farewell#.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go on, then! I'll save the rest for #supper#. | Right you are. Next time, #address#.
line @1 ack : #bc_it_is# | #bc_i_know#
scene the_ewe_again
when topic=memories|smalltalk
does tell.story / react.story / insist / ack
a : Did I ever tell you about #ewe# in #mud#? Up to my chest, I was. | There was a ewe once, stuck fast in a ditch, and I went in after her. Did I tell you? | You'll like this. The day #mud# took a boot off me and I came home with #ewe# instead.
b : You did. Twice. | You told me. At the market. | I've heard it. You lost a boot.
a : Well, it's a good one! It wants telling twice. #saying#. | Did I tell you she bit me after? That bit's new. Sort of. | The left boot. It's still down there, I'd say, #oath#.
b : #bc_ha# | Go on, then. | #bc_fair_enough#

scene the_fair_pig
when topic=pastimes|memories|festival
does tell.story / react.story / insist / ack
a : At #fair# once the prize pig got loose and I caught it by the tail. Have I told you? | You know the pig at #fair#? The one that got loose? That was me caught it. | #pig.capitalize#, the summer it ran through the cake tent. I've told you, haven't I?
b : Every summer. | You have. By the tail. | Only every time I see you.
a : And every summer it's true! #oath#, that pig was fast. | By the tail, and dragged the length of the field. Worth it, mind. | Well, I'll tell you again next time, and you'll smile again. #saying#.
b : #bc_ha# | #bc_go_on# | #bc_ha#

scene the_night_walk
when topic=memories|pastimes self.likes=long_walks
does tell.story / react.story / assess
a : The first warm night of a year, I walked all night after #fair# and watched the sun come up over the barley. Did I say? | You know my story of the night walk? Home from #fair# by starlight, the long way. | I walked home once the whole length of #uproad#, all night, and never met a soul. I've told you that one.
b : You've said. It sounds lovely. | Tell it again, then. | You have. Never a soul.
a : It was. I'd walk it again tonight if they'd let me off #loft#. | The owls, and the dew coming up, and nobody but me. #good#, every step of it. | Not one. Only a hare, and I talked to that. It didn't mind.

scene market_loud
when topic=day|pastimes here.day=market self.likes=market_bustle
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #market.capitalize#! I love it. Everybody shouting and nobody listening. | #market.capitalize#. I've had three talks and a pie, and it's not noon. | You can't hear yourself think at #market#, and I don't want to.
b : It's loud, all right. | Three already? | I like a quiet day.
a : Loud's good! Loud means folk are out, #address#. | And three more before dark, if I'm lucky. #oath#. | I don't. I go home when there's nobody left to talk to.

scene coat_off
when topic=weather|season here.season=spring here.weather=clear self.likes=first_warm_day
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #warmday.capitalize#! Coat off, sleeves up, and I've not stopped grinning. | Feel that sun? The first warm one. I could walk to the coast in it. | I've been waiting all winter for this. #warmday.capitalize#. Don't let me waste it.
b : It's lovely. | The coast's a long way. | You won't.
a : Lovely as #tart#, and I'll have both today. | Then I'd walk back. That's #walk# done right, #address#. | I'll walk to #farfield# and back at noon. Just because.

scene stuck_fast
when topic=weather|land here.weather=rain self.dislikes=deep_mud
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #rain.capitalize#, and the lane's turned to #mud#. I hate it, #address#. | One step off the path and I'm in to the shin. It sucks your boot right off. | I'd sooner walk ten miles dry than one through #mud#.
b : The fields need it, though. | Mind your boots. | Same here.
a : They do. I'll stay on the stones and let them have it. | I lost one to #mud# once. I've told you. I'm careful now. | Same field! Give me a dry track any day. #saying#.

scene a_long_walk
when topic=pastimes|travel self.likes=long_walks
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : Come Restday I'm going on #walk#. Nowhere. Just out and back. | I walked out to #farfield# yesterday, for no reason at all. | Best thing a wolf can do with a free day is walk it, #address#.
b : Where to? | No reason? | Is it?
a : Nowhere! That's the point of #walk#. You walk till you turn round. | None. I wanted to see what the barley was doing. It was growing. #bc_ha# | It is. You see things. I saw two hares boxing once. That's a tale for another day.
b : #bc_ha# | Fair enough. | You will, I'm sure.

scene tart_warm
when topic=food self.likes=plum_tart
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #tart.capitalize#! Is there anything better? I've never found it. | For #tart# I'd walk clear to the next town. I have, nearly. | There was #tart# at supper last night. I had three slices. I'm not sorry.
b : Not that I know of. | I believe you. | Three?
a : Then we agree, and no more to be said. #good#. | Nearly! I turned back at the ford. Smelled the bakery. | Three. And I'd have had a fourth but somebody took it. #manners.capitalize#, some folk.

scene learning_swing
when topic=work self.apprentice=yes self.job=farmer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'm still learning #scythe#. The farmer says I swing like I'm talking. Too much, too wide. | Did I tell you I'm learning #scythe# now? Proper learning, from #boss#. | You have to let #scythe# do the work. I keep forgetting and doing it myself.
b : Do you? | How's it going? | Hard to learn?
a : I do! I can't help it. Wide swings and wide talk, both. | Slow. But I've only cut my own boot once. #oath#. | Hard enough. A season more, they say, and I'll have it. #saying#.

scene granary_day
when topic=work self.working=yes self.job=farmer
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Sacks all morning up to #loft#. My arms are long as a ladder now. | We turned the grain in #loft# today. Hot work, and dusty, and I talked the whole way through. | #self.trade_words.capitalize#, and today that means sacks. Tomorrow too.
b : Sounds heavy. | I bet they loved that. | Sacks are sacks.
a : Heavy, but good. You feel it in your sleep. | They did! Well. Some of them. Mostly they sang louder. | Sacks are sacks. But I count them out loud, and that makes them go quicker, #address#.

scene stooks_up
when topic=harvest|season here.season=summer|autumn self.job=farmer
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #work.capitalize#! Every paw in the fields from dawn, and me the loudest of them. | We got the last of the barley in before dark. #good# work, all of us. | #tired.capitalize#, the lot of us, and still the stooks keep coming.
b : Good to have it in. | Well done. | It'll be over soon.
a : It is! I'll sleep a week in #bed# after. Or a night. One night. | Thank you! You'll hear every sheaf of it from me. #bc_ha# | It will. Then there's the supper, and I'll talk right through that too.

scene my_spouse
when topic=family|home self.married=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : My #self.spouse_word# says I talk enough for two. I say that's why we're married. | #self.spouse# heard all three of my tales the first week. Stayed anyway. #oath#. | I'm a lucky wolf, #address#. I married somebody who'll still listen to me.
b : There's truth in that. | That's love. | You are.
a : There is! One talks, one listens. It works. | It is. Or deafness. I don't ask. | I am. I tell #self.spouse# so most days. Out loud.

scene good_friend
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #self.friend# is #good# company, and patient with me. That's a rare pair. | I'd trust #self.friend# with anything. Even my stories, and I'm careful with those. | #self.friend# and me go back a good way. I'd not swap that for anything.
b : That's worth a lot. | Careful? You? | You're lucky.
a : It is. More than #wages#, anyway. | Careful who I tell them to! Not careful how often. #bc_ha# | I am. I'll say so to anybody who'll stand still.

scene no_manners
when topic=smalltalk|quarrel self.dislikes=bad_manners
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Somebody shoved by me at the well this morning without a word. #manners.capitalize#. | I can't abide #manners#. A good morning costs nothing, #address#. | I held the gate for a wolf today and got a grunt. #manners.capitalize#!
b : There's always one. | It doesn't. | Rude.
a : There is. I say good morning twice as loud to them, just to see. | Not a pip. I say mine anyway, even to the rude ones. | Rude! I told everybody in #loft# about it, too.

scene up_the_road
when topic=family|memories here.season=winter
does tell.feeling / sympathise / assess
a : Come winter I catch myself looking up #uproad#. I couldn't tell you why, #address#. | Hard winters frighten me. I don't say it much. I'm saying it now. | When the snow's on #uproad# I look along it every evening. Old habit.
b : Winters can be cruel. | I'm glad you said it. | Habits are like that.
a : They can. I'll talk about something else in a minute. Just not yet. | So am I. It's quieter in me now. Thank you. | They are. I'll keep this one, I think. #bc_i_will#

scene lean_pay
when topic=times|prices world.times=hard|lean
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : My #wages# don't stretch to the end of the week now. I've stopped telling #tales# for a pie. | Lean times. #tart.capitalize# is a treat now, not a habit. That's how I know. | I'd talk less if I were hungry, they say. I'm still talking. I'm a bit #hungry#, too.
b : It's hard everywhere. | That's a sorry sign. | You'll never stop.
a : It is. Nobody up the hill sees it, though. #grumble#. | It is. I'll have tart again come a better harvest. #saying#. | I won't. Talk's the one thing that's still free.

scene they_say
when topic=gossip
does tell.gossip / react.news / assess
a : You've heard? #topic.subject# #topic.claim#! I had it at the granary. | Listen, #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. Everybody in #loft# is saying so. | I'll tell you what I heard, plain: #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. That's the lot.
b : Is it true? | Everybody's saying? | Thanks for telling me.
a : I don't know. That's what was said, and I've said it back to you, no more. | Everybody I talked to in #loft#, and I talked to everybody. | #deflect#. I'd have burst if I kept it in.

scene fair_coming
when topic=festival world.festival=soon
does tell.plan / react.self / assess
a : #fair.capitalize#'s nearly here! I'll be at every stall twice. | Not long now. I'll walk there the long way, for the joy of it. | Festival soon. Somebody will hear about #pig# who's never heard it. I'll find them.
b : Every stall? | The long way? | Poor soul.
a : Twice! Once to look and once to talk. #oath#. | Over the far field and round by the ford. Takes an hour longer. Best hour. | Lucky soul, you mean! It's a good story, #address#.

scene before_light
when topic=day|work here.time=dawn self.working=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Out before the sun. The barley's wet to the knee and I'm talking to it already. | #greet#! First one in #loft# this morning. That never happens. | First light. Cold paws, hot tea, and a whole day of telling ahead.
b : Talking to barley? | Well done. | Sounds a good start.
a : It doesn't mind. It's the best listener in town, #address#. | Don't tell #boss#. I'll want it every day now. | It is. #good# start, and I'll ruin it by noon with talking.

scene work_going
when topic=newcomer
does tell.worry / react.self / assess
a : #topic.subject# is new, I hear. I hope there's work enough for everybody. | Another newcomer, #topic.subject#. #loft.capitalize# can only take so many, #address#. | #topic.subject.capitalize# has come to stay, they say. I'll be civil. I'm always civil.
b : There's usually enough. | It'll sort itself out. | Good of you.
a : Usually. Not always. I've seen it go short. | Maybe. I'll still be first in #loft# tomorrow, to be safe. | It costs nothing. Unlike #manners#, which costs everybody.

story ewe_in_the_ditch [topic=memories self.age>=18]
  : There was #ewe# stuck in the ditch past the barn, bleating like the sky was falling, and nobody near but me.
  : I went in after her. #mud.capitalize#, up to my chest. It took my left boot, and I let it.
  : I got her out, and she walked off without a look. Not a thank you. I came home in one boot.
  ask : Tell me true, now: in after her, or not?
  b : I'd have thought about it a long while first.
  b[job=farmer|herder] : Every time. You don't leave a ewe in a ditch.

story pig_at_the_fair [topic=pastimes|festival|memories self.age>=18]
  : At #fair# one summer the prize pig got out of its pen and went straight through the cake tent.
  : Everybody screamed and ran. I didn't. I grabbed #pig# by the tail, and it dragged me the length of the field.
  : They gave me a slice of the cake it hadn't trodden on. The best cake I ever had.
  b : By the tail! Did it bite you?
  : Never even looked back. It wanted the cakes, not me. #bc_ha#

story night_walk_home [topic=memories|pastimes self.age>=18 self.likes=long_walks]
  : The first warm night one spring, I walked home from #fair# the long way, all night.
  : Owls overhead, the dew rising, and the barley silver as far as I could see.
  : Just as I got to the lane, the sun came up behind me. I stood there and couldn't say a word.
  ask : Can you picture me with nothing to say?
  b : No. That must have been some sunrise.
  b[pair.band=friends|family] : Not for a moment. That's how I know it's true.

rule @market_cry
when concept=bark here.day=market self.likes=market_bustle
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Pies! Somebody's selling pies at #market#. | #market.capitalize#, and me with an empty belly. #oath#.

rule @mud_bark
when concept=bark here.weather=rain self.dislikes=deep_mud
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Off the path, off the path! #mud.capitalize#. | There goes my boot again. #annoyed#.

rule @warm_bark
when concept=bark here.season=spring here.weather=clear self.likes=first_warm_day
does aside
cooldown 12h
say Coat off! Coat off, it's #warmday#. | Feel that sun. #bc_lovely#

rule @scythe_bark
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=farmer
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Let #scythe# do it. Let it do it. | Swing, step, swing. Don't talk. Don't talk.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#! What can I tell you? I know plenty. | #greet#, #address#! Stop a while. I'll talk if you will.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#! Back again. Have I told you about the pig? | #topic.player#! Good. I've a story you'll like, if I haven't told you.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=farmer] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. Sacks to #loft#, rows to cut, and learning #scythe# when they let me. | Fields, mostly. And talking. Mostly talking, #boss# says.
dlg @2 resident.job : #job_busy# Whatever wants doing, loudly. | Odd jobs, #address#, with a story for each one.
dlg @1 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : #news_none# Not even at the granary, and that's saying something. | Nothing new, #address#. Only my three stories, and you've heard those.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : #gossip_none# For once I've nothing to pass on. | Nothing about anybody. I'm as surprised as you.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#! I'll tell you the rest next time. | #farewell#! Come back, I'll have a new one. I won't, but come back.
graft resident.hub
choice I hear you tell a good story. Tell me one. -> tale
node tale
say Do I! Pick one: #ewe# in the ditch, the pig at the fair, or the night I walked home till dawn. They're all true, every word.
mood keen
free
choice The pig at the fair. -> tale_pig
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node tale_pig
say #pig.capitalize# got out and went through the cake tent. I caught it by the tail and it dragged me the length of the field.
choice Ha! Thank you. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
